BUILD LATER (filed 2026-08-04, Zach-directed): give senechal an ISSUE front door plus its drain. Decision settled 2026-08-04: an account writes only its OWN repo; anything crossing a project boundary is filed as a GitHub issue and drained by the owner. This resolves realisateur/MONKEY.md 8.1, where notify-senechal is structurally impossible from a self-dev account -- the front door PUSHES to hf7y/senechal and every self-dev account holds a read-only deploy key there on purpose, so installe exits 8 on every verb install (ecosim is affected identically, unnoticed). TWO HALVES, and the second is the one not to skip: (1) notify-senechal gains an issue path, filing a labelled notice issue on hf7y/senechal -- cheap, because scheduler/bin/scheduler already creates labelled issues, lists open ones, comments answers and applies labels (the machinery ecosim's #26/#27 used). (2) A DRAIN running AS senechal (which can push senechal) that pulls notice issues into .scheduler/FOCUS.md and closes them. Without the drain, notes pile up unread -- build-but-do-not-wire. Same shape as bibliothecaire draining its own request queue. NOT a mail bus: an email has no labels, and the labels ARE the protocol.
